"Let $\\mathcal{C}_5^3$ be the $3$-uniform tight cycle of length $5$, with vertex set $\\{1,\\dots,5\\}$ and edges of the form $\\{x,x+1,x+2\\pmod 5\\}$. Let $\\pi(\\mathcal{C}_5^3)$ denote its Turán density. **Mubayi–Rödl conjecture.**\n\n$$\n\\pi(\\mathcal{C}_5^3)=2\\sqrt{3}-3.\n$$\n\nThe conjecture is attributed to Mubayi and Rödl and is presented as a central open problem on tight-cycle Turán densities; the paper proves results for sufficiently long tight cycles but does not settle the length-$5$ case."